The qualifications for a valid Malibu lemon law claim are:

- The manufacturer has made a reasonable number of attempts (at least two) to fix a significant defect covered under warranty.

- Your vehicle has been out of service for 30 or more cumulative days for warranty-covered repairs.

- The vehicle’s defects are not the result of driver abuse, improper use, neglect, or unauthorized modifications.

