## Frequently Asked Questions

## What qualifies a vehicle under Malibu lemon law?

A vehicle sold with a manufacturer or dealer warranty may qualify for benefits under Malibu lemon law. Any defect must be officially reported to the manufacturer within the terms of the warranty to be eligible for a lemon law claim - if the repair facility is unable to fix the issue.

## Can I file a Malibu lemon law claim without an attorney?

Yes, you are free to file a lemon law claim with the manufacturer without an attorney. However, seeking fair compensation will be very difficult, even if you believe the claim is valid. Manufacturers work with high-powered defense teams to deny or minimize the payout for lemon law claims. These teams use many different tactics to avoid responsibility for selling defective products.

A skilled Malibu lemon law lawyer manages the negotiation process with these legal teams to fight for every dollar you are rightfully owed.

## What is the time limit to file a Malibu lemon law claim?

California has a four-year statute of limitations to file a lemon law claim. We recommend NOT waiting four years to start the process. The longer you wait, the more difficult negotiations become. If you believe you have a defective vehicle, get in touch with a Malibu lemon law attorney immediately to take the next steps.

## What if I want a lemon law replacement instead of a buyback?

Some consumers choose to remain loyal to their chosen car brand after being sold a defective vehicle - and pursue a replacement vehicle via the state’s lemon law. These replacements must be the same vehicle or one of equal value.

In lemon law claims, manufacturers are not required to provide replacement vehicles (unlike a buyback). Both you and the automaker must mutually agree to these terms.

## Does Malibu lemon law apply to private car sales?

In most cases, private car sales are done under an implied “as is” agreement - meaning there are no warranty protections in place should it be defective.

## How long does it take to settle a Malibu lemon law case?

Most Malibu lemon law cases can be completed within a couple of months - but some can take longer given the circumstances. No two lemon law claims are the same. The timeline depends on the complexity of the defect and the manufacturer’s negotiation tactics.
